# ForestProof project rule

Read the repository root AGENTS.md, docs/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md, docs/PROJECT_MAP.md, PROJECT_BRAIN.md, and execution/CURRENT_STATUS.md before substantial work.

The project converts sourced environmental observations into reviewable evidence, human-authorized investigation/action, and follow-up outcomes. DEMO data is synthetic. Never assert illegality, current live monitoring, causal impact, or production readiness without verification.

The original prompts in docs/origin are historical source material, not current executable instructions or verified facts. Current user direction and implementation/status evidence take precedence.

The owner prefers Codex Cloud, no local-Docker prerequisite, and OVH for eventual production hosting. No OVH deployment has been verified; Railway docs are historical. Do not deploy or incur recurring costs without current authorization.

Keep documentation aligned with code and clearly label WORKING, PARTIAL, PLANNED, BLOCKED, DEFERRED, and DOCUMENTED_NOT_TESTED.
